.TH SAMBA-ADWS 1 "September 2026" "samba-adws 1.0.1" "HardenSamba"
.SH NAME
samba-adws \- Active Directory Web Services for Samba: run, check, or query the service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B samba-adws run
.br
.B samba-adws check
.br
.BR "samba-adws patch-samba " [ \-\-check | \-\-no-install | \-\-revert ]
.br
.B samba-adws \-\-version
.br
.BI "samba-adws naming-context \-\-server " controller
.br
.BI "samba-adws search \-\-server " controller " \-\-base " dn " [" options "]"
.br
.BI "samba-adws new-user \-\-server " controller " \-\-parent " dn " \-\-rdn " rdn " \-\-sam " name " [" options "]"
.br
.BI "samba-adws set-password \-\-server " controller " \-\-identity " dn
.br
.B samba-adws status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B samba-adws
is the command the samba-adws module declares. The service itself is
.BR samba-adws.service ,
which listens on tcp/9389 and answers the WS-* protocols the ActiveDirectory
PowerShell module, the Active Directory Administrative Center and the rest of
RSAT speak. This command is the way an operator runs that service in the
foreground, checks the installation, or reads the directory from Linux.
.SH VERBS
.TP
.B run
Runs the service in the foreground, reading the same configuration files the
unit reads. Useful when systemd has reported a failure and not its cause.
.TP
.B check
Checks the installation: Python imports, the local directory, and the handler
routing. Prints one line per check and a summary.
.TP
.B patch-samba
Rebuilds Debian's samba source package with the one patch that makes the
controller announce ADWS in its CLDAP netlogon reply, installs the result at a
local version, adds "adws:advertise = yes" to smb.conf, restarts samba-ad-dc
and reads the reply back. The Active Directory Administrative Center, and the
PowerShell cmdlets used without \-Server, only find controllers that announce,
and stock Samba never does. Needs root, deb-src lines (added if missing),
about 4 GB under /var/tmp and tens of minutes.
.B \-\-check
reports the state and changes nothing;
.B \-\-no-install
builds and verifies only;
.B \-\-revert
puts the stock packages back. A Debian security update of samba replaces the
rebuilt packages; run it again afterwards.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Prints the module version from MODULE.yaml.
.TP
.BI "naming-context \-\-server " controller
Prints, as JSON, the default naming context the controller publishes, which is
where a caller starts before it holds any distinguished name.
.TP
.BI "search \-\-server " controller " \-\-base " dn
Prints one page of the objects under a container, as JSON. See
.B samba-adws search \-\-help
for the scope, filter, property and page-size options.
.TP
.BI "new-user \-\-server " controller " \-\-parent " dn " \-\-rdn " rdn " \-\-sam " name
Creates a user account under
.IR dn ,
gives it the password read from standard input, then enables it, in that order,
and prints its distinguished name, objectGUID and the step it reached as JSON.
A failure after the create leaves the account disabled and says so. See
.B samba-adws new-user \-\-help
for the optional name attributes.
.TP
.BI "set-password \-\-server " controller " \-\-identity " dn
Sets the password of the account
.IR dn
to the one read from standard input.
.IP
Both write verbs read the password from standard input, one line, or without
echo when standard input is a terminal; neither takes it as an argument. Both
run as the Kerberos principal in the caller's credential cache, and the
controller refuses a write that principal has no right to.
.TP
.B status
Prints, as JSON, the module name, its version and the verbs it answers. Opens
no connection; a consumer uses it to ask whether this command answers at all.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hardensamba/samba-adws/samba-adws.conf
The service's configuration, a conffile: the address and port, the log file
and level, and the message-size ceiling.
.TP
.I /etc/default/samba-adws
Read first if present, for an installation that came from the from-checkout
installer; the conffile above wins where both name a variable.
.TP
.I /usr/share/samba-adws
The service and the client, installed as a payload rather than into the
Python path.
.TP
.I /var/log/samba-adws/adws.log
The service's log, in a directory systemd creates for it.
.TP
.I /var/lib/samba-adws/samba-patched
Written by patch-samba: the samba version it last rebuilt and when.
.TP
.I /var/tmp/samba-adws-patch/
Where patch-samba builds; the packages, build.log and install.log stay there.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
The client verbs authenticate with Kerberos from the current ticket cache; run
.B kinit
first. Every request runs on the controller as the principal that
authenticated it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR samba-tool (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
and the documentation under
.IR /usr/share/doc/samba-adws/documentation/ .
